llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: MOVD/MOVQ between general and vector registers carry no execution domain (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for a vector register loaded by movd or
movq and then stored or combined: the execution-domain fix no longer turns
the following move into its integer form. r288902 (Simon Pilgrim,
2016-12-07, "[X86][SSE] Consistently set MOVD/MOVQ load/store/move
instructions to integer domain", llvm-project 8893bd95f015, D27419, first
release LLVM 4.0) put six groups of X86InstrSSE.td in SSEPackedInt; 3.9 left
them in the default domain. This patch takes back that file's part of the
commit exactly (the AVX-512 file is not used by btver2 and is left). In the
game region a `vmovd` of a general register into a vector register is
followed directly by a `vmovaps` store 376 times and by a `vmovdqa` store
once; 4.0.0 gives `vmovdqa` (the lane-mask constant of the 325 per-file
static initializers: `mov eax, -1; vmovd xmm2, eax; vmovaps [mask], xmm2`),
the prebuilt 3.6.2 to 3.9.1 give `vmovaps` (round 189A). No source form
changes the store's domain. With this patch the twelve initializers in the
tree store with `vmovaps` and no matched game row and no draft changes (the
supervisor's module sweep).

